A host loads a linked extension through the file its link points at now.

Handed the link, jiti resolves the extension's own imports through the copy
it first loaded. A host outlives the moves of the link an extension is found
through, so once that link moves, a hosted /reload runs the new entry against
the old copy's helpers, or fails with ENOENT once the old copy is gone. Only
the import takes the real path: the extension cache and the managed-proxy
check stay keyed by the link, and a reload's new cache token empties the
cache.

